# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF. For anything that a Linux container executes that
# is fatal and the error is unhelpful: `#!/bin/sh\r` makes the kernel look for
# an interpreter literally named "sh\r", and the container dies with
# "no such file or directory" while pointing at a file that plainly exists.
#
# docker/docker-entrypoint.d/25-basic-auth.sh is exactly that case - without
# this rule the dashboard container fails to start on a fresh clone.
*.sh text eol=lf
